# Task 10: Playwright storageState files are live session cookies for the
# 20-user fixture (e2e/fixtures/auth.setup.ts) — credential material, not
# source, and regenerated fresh on every `npm run test:e2e` run.
/e2e/fixtures/.auth/

# Agent-tooling scratch directories. These hold working material for the
# assistants that build this project — briefs, ledgers, per-task reports,
# plugin caches. None of it is source, and none of it is meaningful to anyone
# reading the repository.
#
# Ignored at the ROOT rather than by a nested .gitignore inside each directory:
# a nested file only protects a subtree that already exists, so a newly
# installed plugin writing to a new top-level path is unprotected until someone
# notices. /.impeccable/ is exactly that case — the plugin was installed on
# 2026-08-17 and writes hook.cache.json into the project root.
#
# Note the standing hazard, recorded because it has already cost this project
# real work: material under these paths is INVISIBLE to review and is destroyed
# by `git clean -fdx`. A regression probe for D-185 was lost that way. If
# something here becomes evidence for a claim, commit it somewhere else first —
# never cite a path under an ignored directory from a commit message or a code
# comment (see docs/COMMIT_CONVENTION.md and register row D-207).
/.superpowers/
/.impeccable/

# Working material for the team and its tooling — deliberately NOT in this
# repository. A repository holds the software and what is needed to build, run,
# review and operate it. It is not a filing cabinet for planning notes, audit
# transcripts, agent instructions, or a project-management ledger.
#
# These files remain on disk (the tooling reads them) and are version-controlled
# separately in ../toolkit-process.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
/docs/SKILLS_INVENTORY.md
/docs/DEFERRED_REGISTER.md
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/planning/
/docs/audits/
